INT. TIRYNS - THRONE ROOM - DAY

EURYSTHEUS sits on his throne. HERCULES stands before him. The lion lies on the floor.

EURYSTHEUS
Hercules, son of Zeus and Alcmene, I am Eurystheus, King of Tiryns. As you know, Hera made me king by delaying your birth, and the oracle at Delphi has told you that you must serve me for twelve years to purify yourself of the terrible crime you committed against your wife Megara and your children.

HERCULES
Yes, King Eurystheus. As you know, I am the strongest man alive, and I killed the Nemean Lion with my bare hands because it could not be pierced by weapons. I was driven mad by Hera, who has hated me since I strangled two serpents in my cradle.

EURYSTHEUS
That is correct. Hera is the queen of the gods and she is jealous of Zeus. I am afraid of you, so I will give you ten labors to complete.

HERCULES
I will do whatever you ask.

EURYSTHEUS
Good. (laughs) Your wife must be glad she's dead, ha ha, so she doesn't have to watch you serve me.

HERCULES
(laughs) Yes!

EURYSTHEUS
The next labor is the Lernaean Hydra. Go and kill it.

HERCULES
I will do it.

ATHENA appears in a flash of light.

ATHENA
Hello, Hercules. I am Athena, goddess of wisdom. I want everyone to know that Hera is plotting against you and that the gods are watching. Good luck!

Hercules leaves.
